{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "6be8ed10",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Exercise — Effect of Gradient Strength on Image Geometry\n",
    "\n",
    "So far, we have assumed that the gradient produced by the MRI scanner is exactly the gradient that we requested.\n",
    "\n",
    "But what if the actual gradient strength is slightly different?\n",
    "\n",
    "During frequency encoding, position is related to frequency by\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\Delta f(x) = \\bar{\\gamma} G_x x\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "where:\n",
    "\n",
    "- $x$ is the spatial position,\n",
    "- $G_x$ is the frequency-encoding gradient,\n",
    "- $\\bar{\\gamma}$ is the gyromagnetic ratio in Hz/T.\n",
    "\n",
    "In this exercise, we will assume that the gradient remains perfectly **linear**, but its strength is slightly different from the expected value.\n",
    "\n",
    "We will investigate how this affects the geometry of the same digital phantom used earlier."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "20a7c278",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 1. Define the gradient error\n",
    "\n",
    "Suppose we request a frequency-encoding gradient of\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "G_{\\mathrm{nominal}} = 20\\ \\mathrm{mT/m}.\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "However, the scanner produces only **90%** of the requested gradient.\n",
    "\n",
    "Therefore,\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "G_{\\mathrm{actual}}\n",
    "=\n",
    "0.90\\,G_{\\mathrm{nominal}}.\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "Calculate the actual gradient strength."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "fb297e37",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 2. How does the gradient affect frequency encoding?\n",
    "\n",
    "For a linear frequency-encoding gradient,\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\Delta f(x) = \\bar{\\gamma}G_xx.\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "The proton gyromagnetic ratio is approximately\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\bar{\\gamma} = 42.58 \\times 10^6\\ \\mathrm{Hz/T}.\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "Let's calculate the frequency offset across our phantom for both:\n",
    "\n",
    "- the nominal gradient, and\n",
    "- the actual gradient.\n",
    "\n",
    "Both gradients are still linear.\n",
    "\n",
    "The only difference is their **strength**."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "eb94c8f4",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Observe the frequency encoding\n",
    "\n",
    "Both frequency-position relationships are straight lines.\n",
    "\n",
    "However, the actual gradient has a smaller slope.\n",
    "\n",
    "Therefore, at the same physical position,\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "|\\Delta f_{\\mathrm{actual}}|\n",
    "<\n",
    "|\\Delta f_{\\mathrm{nominal}}|.\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "In other words, a weaker gradient produces a smaller frequency shift for the same spatial position.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Think before continuing\n",
    "\n",
    "Consider a spin located at\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "x_{\\mathrm{true}} = 50\\ \\mathrm{mm}.\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "If the actual gradient is only 90% of the expected gradient, the measured frequency will also be smaller than expected.\n",
    "\n",
    "But the reconstruction still assumes that the gradient was $20$ mT/m.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Where will the reconstruction think this spin is located?**\n",
    "\n",
    "Make a prediction before running the next cell."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "c4a52c89",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 3. Why did the position change?\n",
    "\n",
    "The spin was actually located at\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "x_{\\mathrm{true}} = 50\\ \\mathrm{mm},\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "but it was reconstructed at\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "x_{\\mathrm{recon}} = 45\\ \\mathrm{mm}.\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "Let's understand why.\n",
    "\n",
    "The reconstruction converts the measured frequency back into position using the **nominal gradient**:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "x_{\\mathrm{recon}}\n",
    "=\n",
    "\\frac{\\Delta f_{\\mathrm{measured}}}\n",
    "{\\bar{\\gamma}G_{\\mathrm{nominal}}}.\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "However, the measured frequency was actually generated by the **actual gradient**:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\Delta f_{\\mathrm{measured}}\n",
    "=\n",
    "\\bar{\\gamma}G_{\\mathrm{actual}}x_{\\mathrm{true}}.\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "Substituting this into the reconstruction equation gives\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "x_{\\mathrm{recon}}\n",
    "=\n",
    "\\frac{\n",
    "\\bar{\\gamma}G_{\\mathrm{actual}}x_{\\mathrm{true}}\n",
    "}{\n",
    "\\bar{\\gamma}G_{\\mathrm{nominal}}\n",
    "}.\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "The gyromagnetic ratio cancels:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\boxed{\n",
    "x_{\\mathrm{recon}}\n",
    "=\n",
    "\\frac{G_{\\mathrm{actual}}}\n",
    "{G_{\\mathrm{nominal}}}\n",
    "x_{\\mathrm{true}}\n",
    "}\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "For our experiment,\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\frac{G_{\\mathrm{actual}}}\n",
    "{G_{\\mathrm{nominal}}}\n",
    "=\n",
    "\\frac{18}{20}\n",
    "=\n",
    "0.90.\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "Therefore,\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\boxed{\n",
    "x_{\\mathrm{recon}}\n",
    "=\n",
    "0.90x_{\\mathrm{true}}\n",
    "}\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "Every position along $x$ is reconstructed at 90% of its true position."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "2417d450",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 4. What does this do to an image?\n",
    "\n",
    "Now let's apply the same gradient error to the digital phantom that we have been using throughout the notebook.\n",
    "\n",
    "Only the frequency-encoding gradient $G_x$ is incorrect.\n",
    "\n",
    "Therefore,\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "x_{\\mathrm{recon}} = 0.90x_{\\mathrm{true}},\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "while\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "y_{\\mathrm{recon}} = y_{\\mathrm{true}}.\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "Before running the simulation, make a prediction:\n",
    "\n",
    "**What will happen to the circular structures in our phantom?**\n",
    "\n",
    "Will they:\n",
    "\n",
    "- remain circular?\n",
    "- become narrower along $x$?\n",
    "- become wider along $x$?"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "d223c22f",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 5. Change the gradient\n",
    "\n",
    "Now change the value of `gradient_scale` and observe how the phantom geometry changes.\n",
    "\n",
    "Try values such as:\n",
    "\n",
    "- `1.00`\n",
    "- `0.95`\n",
    "- `0.90`\n",
    "- `0.80`\n",
    "- `1.10`\n",
    "\n",
    "Before running each experiment, predict the result.\n",
    "\n",
    "Remember:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\text{gradient scale}\n",
    "=\n",
    "\\frac{G_{\\mathrm{actual}}}\n",
    "{G_{\\mathrm{nominal}}}.\n",
    "$$"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "8684dbf1",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Questions\n",
    "\n",
    "After trying different gradient strengths, answer the following:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. What happens when\n",
    "\n",
    "   $$\n",
    "   G_{\\mathrm{actual}} < G_{\\mathrm{nominal}}?\n",
    "   $$\n",
    "\n",
    "2. What happens when\n",
    "\n",
    "   $$\n",
    "   G_{\\mathrm{actual}} > G_{\\mathrm{nominal}}?\n",
    "   $$\n",
    "\n",
    "3. What happens when\n",
    "\n",
    "   $$\n",
    "   G_{\\mathrm{actual}} = G_{\\mathrm{nominal}}?\n",
    "   $$\n",
    "\n",
    "4. Why does the geometric change occur only along the $x$-direction?\n",
    "\n",
    "5. Did we remove any k-space samples in this experiment?\n",
    "\n",
    "6. Can an image therefore have incorrect geometry even when the acquired data are otherwise complete?"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "304cce87",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 6. Can we correct the geometric distortion?\n",
    "\n",
    "Suppose we independently measure the gradient and discover that the actual gradient was only 90% of the expected gradient.\n",
    "\n",
    "We know that\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "x_{\\mathrm{recon}}\n",
    "=\n",
    "\\frac{G_{\\mathrm{actual}}}\n",
    "{G_{\\mathrm{nominal}}}\n",
    "x_{\\mathrm{true}}.\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "Therefore,\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "x_{\\mathrm{true}}\n",
    "=\n",
    "\\frac{G_{\\mathrm{nominal}}}\n",
    "{G_{\\mathrm{actual}}}\n",
    "x_{\\mathrm{recon}}.\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "The geometric correction factor is therefore\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "C_x\n",
    "=\n",
    "\\frac{G_{\\mathrm{nominal}}}\n",
    "{G_{\\mathrm{actual}}}.\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "For our example,\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "C_x\n",
    "=\n",
    "\\frac{20}{18}\n",
    "=\n",
    "\\frac{1}{0.90}\n",
    "\\approx 1.11.\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "Let's use this calibration information to restore the phantom geometry."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "5d07310e",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Key observation\n",
    "\n",
    "The gradient in this experiment remained perfectly **linear**.\n",
    "\n",
    "The only problem was that\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "G_{\\mathrm{actual}}\n",
    "\\neq\n",
    "G_{\\mathrm{nominal}}.\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "Because MRI gradients encode spatial position, an error in gradient strength causes measured frequencies to be assigned to incorrect spatial locations.\n",
    "\n",
    "For a uniform gradient calibration error,\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\boxed{\n",
    "x_{\\mathrm{recon}}\n",
    "=\n",
    "\\frac{G_{\\mathrm{actual}}}\n",
    "{G_{\\mathrm{nominal}}}\n",
    "x_{\\mathrm{true}}\n",
    "}\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "Therefore:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "G_{\\mathrm{actual}} < G_{\\mathrm{nominal}}\n",
    "\\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad\n",
    "\\text{compression}\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "and\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "G_{\\mathrm{actual}} > G_{\\mathrm{nominal}}\n",
    "\\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad\n",
    "\\text{expansion}.\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "If the gradient calibration error is known, the geometric scaling can be corrected."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "464d5297",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Think ahead\n",
    "\n",
    "In this simulation:\n",
    "\n",
    "- the gradient error was simple,\n",
    "- the gradient remained linear,\n",
    "- the error occurred only along one direction,\n",
    "- and we knew the exact calibration error.\n",
    "\n",
    "Real MRI systems may not always be this simple.\n",
    "\n",
    "**What would you need to know about the scanner's spatial encoding to correct a more complicated geometric distortion?**\n",
    "\n",
    "Keep this question in mind when we work with the real phantom data acquired on the low-field MRI scanner."
   ]
  }
 ],
